= No.

# ** Kubernetes software depends on one of the containerization software. ex : docker, podman, crio.

# ** 
# kubeadm (install on both master and worker )   -- is a tool the first pepared the master and the joins the worker mode.
# kubelet (install on both master and worker )   -- it is a agent process that runs on every node of kubecluster.
                                                    the agent process starts when we run the kubeadm init master/kubeadm join on worker.

# kubectl (install only master )                 -- it is a client tool, that helps us to create/manage/deploy and delete containers in kube cluster.

# kubeadm init                                   -- start the agent process of kubeadm init master/worker.

